6.Which tag is used for the items inside a `<datalist>`?
A)`<li>`
B)`<item>`
C)`<option>`  //answer
D)`<dt>`

✅ Correct Answer: C. <option>

Explanation (Simple)

The <datalist> element contains <option> elements, which provide suggestions for an <input> field.

Example:
<input list="browsers" name="browser">

<datalist id="browsers">
  <option value="Chrome">
  <option value="Firefox">
  <option value="Edge">
  <option value="Safari">
</datalist>

When the user types in the input box, these <option> values appear as suggestions.

Why not the others?
❌ A. <li> → Used for list items in <ul> or <ol>.
❌ B. <item> → Not a valid HTML tag.
❌ C. <option> → ✅ Correct! Used inside <datalist>.
❌ D. <dt> → Used in a definition list (<dl>).

✅ Correct Answer: C. <option>


