10.How do you change the alignment of the `<legend>` text?
A)`align="center"`
B)CSS `text-align` //answer
C)`pos="top"`
D)`title-align="left"`


✅ Correct Answer: B. CSS text-align

Explanation (Simple)

The <legend> tag is the title of a <fieldset>. To change its alignment, use the CSS text-align property.

Example:
<fieldset>
  <legend style="text-align: center;">Personal Information</legend>
</fieldset>

Or with external CSS:

legend {
  text-align: center;
}
Why not the others?
❌ A. align="center" → Obsolete/deprecated in HTML5.
✅ B. CSS text-align → Correct and recommended.
❌ C. pos="top" → Not a valid HTML attribute.
❌ D. title-align="left" → Not a valid HTML attribute.

✅ Correct Answer: B. CSS text-align